melody:
# Chorus as published in 1927 (cut time, written here with quarter-note beats)
I'm look-ing o-ver a four leaf clo-ver
Bb4(2) F4 D4 C4 Bb3(2) C4 D4(2) F4 Bb4 ~Bb4 A4(2)
that I o-ver-looked be-fore;
Bb4 C5(2) C4 D4 E4(2) G4(2) C5(4) ~C5(4)
one leaf is sun-shine, the sec-ond is rain,
A4(2) G4 F4 A4(2) G4 F4 G4 G4 G4 G4 ~G4(4)
third is the ros-es that grow in the lane.
C5(2) A4 G4 C5(2) A4 G4 F4 F4 F4 F4 ~F4(4)
No need ex-plain-ing, the one re-main-ing
Bb4(2) F4 D4 C4 Bb3(2) C4 D4(2) F4 Bb4 ~Bb4 A4(2)
is some-bod-y I a-dore.
Bb4 C5(2) C4 D4 E4(2) G4(2) C5(4) ~C5(4)
I'm look-ing o-ver a four leaf clo-ver
C5(2) Bb4 A4 C5 Bb4(2) G4 A4(2) A4 A4 ~A4 G4(2)
that I o-ver-looked be-fore.
F4 G4(2) A4 Bb4 C5(2) F4(2) Bb4(4) ~Bb4 r r(2)

# Once more
I'm look-ing o-ver a four leaf clo-ver
Bb4(2) F4 D4 C4 Bb3(2) C4 D4(2) F4 Bb4 ~Bb4 A4(2)
that I o-ver-looked be-fore;
Bb4 C5(2) C4 D4 E4(2) G4(2) C5(4) ~C5(4)
one leaf is sun-shine, the sec-ond is rain,
A4(2) G4 F4 A4(2) G4 F4 G4 G4 G4 G4 ~G4(4)
third is the ros-es that grow in the lane.
C5(2) A4 G4 C5(2) A4 G4 F4 F4 F4 F4 ~F4(4)
No need ex-plain-ing, the one re-main-ing
Bb4(2) F4 D4 C4 Bb3(2) C4 D4(2) F4 Bb4 ~Bb4 A4(2)
is some-bod-y I a-dore.
Bb4 C5(2) C4 D4 E4(2) G4(2) C5(4) ~C5(4)
I'm look-ing o-ver a four leaf clo-ver
C5(2) Bb4 A4 C5 Bb4(2) G4 A4(2) A4 A4 ~A4 G4(2)
